  "long_biography": {
    "plain_text": "As president of Bondy's Ford, David Hall Marshall described the limits of a routine trade-in appraisal. His dealership used inspections and test drives to assess vehicles before agreeing an allowance against a customer's next purchase. A standard appraisal did not involve removing the interior trim; suspected water damage called for closer investigation.\n\nThe business began when his parents-in-law, Fred and Frances Bondy, bought Malone Motor Company. They relocated it to Ross Clark Circle and established the Bondy's name. Frances remained involved for more than four decades. Away from work, Marshall enjoyed weekends at the beach listening to the Bee Gees.",
